  "id": "COMPOUND:25647 - PROTEIN:5866",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Dihydroartemisinic acid may be associated with NCI-H446 through a series of target relationships. The compound is identified as a target of MIP, which in turn is a target of NCI-H446 in two distinct pathways. In one pathway, MIP is targeted by [(2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-4,5-dihydroxy-3,6-bis(3-nitropropanoyloxy)oxan-2-yl]methyl 3-nitropropanoate, while in another pathway, MIP is targeted by 5-Hydroxytryptophan monohydrate, dl-. Both of these intermediates ultimately target NCI-H446. The consistent presence of MIP as a common target across these pathways indicates a potential mechanism by which Dihydroartemisinic acid may influence NCI-H446. The evidence supports a possible role for Dihydroartemisinic acid in modulating NCI-H446 through the interaction with MIP, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
